#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Audit client MCP compatibility with separate evidence levels.

The default mode reads declarations and Atenea's effective profile policy.
Missing disk declarations do not prove that a wrapper failed to inject them.
--live discovers each profile directly, recording server version and schema hash;
it does not claim to observe the tools a host delivered to its model.
--wire captures a supported client's request through a loopback recorder.
Historical counts are observations, never compatibility requirements.

Usage: mcp-agree [--live|--wire] [--client=NAME] [--profile=NAME] [--quiet]
       mcp-agree --trust-warning
Exit: 0 verified requested wire measurement; 1 detected conflict or failed probe;
      2 invalid input or unreadable configuration; 3 incomplete evidence.
"""

